#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0102 expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "ADLBC WITHOUT APERIOD -- Requirements.Variables.All [APERIOD] (PLAN-join-key-authoring-gate §3b, as the CDISC siblings author it) skips the rule: APERIOD is a `not empty()` conjunct AND the driver of the constructed ADSL.TRTxxP name of the bound $trt_p (concat(\"ADSL.TRT\", printf(\"%02d\", APERIOD), \"P\")), so without it the rule cannot name what it tests. Re-pinned from the PIN-TODAY `noViolation` (AD0102-F1: a SILENT no-finding by broadcast fold) — non-executability is a skip, not a pass. Was PMDA-AD0102-valid_no_aperiod_column-ADLBC.cdt."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
---
S1 | 001 | GLUC | 5.1
---

